<title>USA: Black &amp; Decker wins patent lawsuit.</title>
<headline>Black &amp; Decker wins patent lawsuit.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Black &amp; Decker Corp said Monday a federal court jury in Virginia ruled in its favor on August 23 and awarded it $3.7 million in a patent infringement suit brought against Coleman Co Inc.</p>
<p>The patent dispute involved Black &amp; Decker's &quot;SnakeLight&quot; flexible flashlight.</p>
<p>Black &amp; Decker claimed its product was infringed by a Coleman product imported from China.</p>
<p>Reuters Chicago Newsdesk - 312-408-8787</p>
